  "openFindings": [
    {
      "id": "C3-WORLD-E04",
      "severity": "P1",
      "status": "OPEN_ON_IMMUTABLE_002",
      "title": "Native tribute-selection constraints on equal-rank suit order and physical-copy ties are omitted from the representation-gap filter.",
      "location": {
        "path": "/Users/ccrt/game/guandan/lab/review6/visible-world.ts",
        "function": "exchangeRepresentationGaps",
        "predicate": "rankOrder(candidate.rank)>rankOrder(gift.rank)"
      },
      "provenance": "Independent conserved108-card second-round engine fixtures with actual applyTribute, completeReturn and a full2-action public prefix. No neural scores or teacher values. The two roots differ only in the known tribute origin/identity and resulting native own-card order; actor own physical set, represented state and per-action399 inputs match.",
      "reproduction": [
        "Construct the genuine previous public result [0,3,1,2], levelsAfter[3,2], and second round. Place every eligible higher-than-A card under actor0 so no strictly higher hidden card exists. Actor0/giver2 pre-exchange holdings are arranged so the actual gift is either S-A#12 or C-A#51; after the gift both actor own physical sets are identical.",
        "Execute the recorded legal D2 return, play thatD2 from giver2 and let seat3 pass. Current actor0, full public action history,331 vector and399 candidate-feature set are identical across the two roots. Each root reports representationGaps=[].",
        "In the S-A public-gift case, a C-A twin#105 in the foreign giver hand would precede S-A under the native sorted tie rule, so that allocation cannot reproduce the recorded gift. In the C-A case the same twin can be present, with actual identical-copy selection/rejection.",
        "32 fixed caller seeds find giver2 holding C-A#105 in0 S-gift worlds versus11 C-gift worlds. The support difference follows the frozen canonical rule, not the finite frequency alone. The public gift constraint is absent from the331 representation and the current filter only tests strictly higher rank."
      ],
      "proof": {
        "actor": 0,
        "sameOwnPhysicalSet": true,
        "samePublicActionHistory": true,
        "sameModel331": true,
        "same399CandidateInputSet": true,
        "gapFlags": [
