          },
          {
            "from": 2,
            "to": 0,
            "card": {
              "id": 51,
              "suit": "C",
              "rank": 14
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "impact": "The sampler correctly conditions on public native gift selection, but the empty-gap eligibility filter admits roots whose conditional hidden-world belief depends on unencoded public information. This defeats the intended conservative representation boundary before any strong pilot labels. No downstream value or outcome difference was measured.",
      "requestedClosure": [
        "Flag unresolved foreign-giver canonical selection constraints, including equal-power earlier-suit resources and identical rank/suit copy-selection probabilities, not only strictly higher ranks.",
        "Account for already fixed own/public pre-exchange ownership and public transfer chains so fully known cases remain eligible. Keep foreign copy ties sampled and rejected honestly; do not force the recorded foreign copy or weaken native ordering.",
        "Use the full portable witness to assert that these two previously empty-gap roots are flagged/excluded before strong label generation. Do not use outcome-based eligibility tuning."
      ],
